@@ -98,7 +98,19 @@ ### Ticket
 
 **Immutability enforcement:** the write-once rule is enforced on the `Ticket` model (`updating` hook), so it applies to Eloquent saves only — mass updates through the query builder (`Ticket::query()->update(...)`) bypass it and must not be used on issued tickets.
 
-**Single-ticket call (scope note):** `Ticket::call()` marks one waiting ticket as `called` (entity-membership checked, exactly-once). This minimal domain primitive proves the mutable `status`/`called_*` fields; deterministic call-next selection (priority + age + 3-ticket fairness) and HTTP/Livewire panels remain out of scope per #14.
+**Single-ticket call:** `Ticket::call()` marks one waiting ticket as `called` (entity-membership checked, exactly-once). This minimal domain primitive proves the mutable `status`/`called_*` fields.
+
+**Call-next selection:** `App\Actions\CallNextTicket` implements the deterministic selection behind the attendant call panel. It is constructed without arguments and invoked as `__invoke(Queue $queue, User $calledBy, CallMode $mode = CallMode::Any): Ticket`, where `CallMode` is the string-backed enum `App\Enums\CallMode` (`any`, `priority_only`, `normal_only`). It rejects inactive queues (re-reading queue state from the database inside the transaction, locking the queue row) with `App\Exceptions\InactiveQueueException`, and throws `App\Exceptions\NoWaitingTicketsException` when no ticket is eligible for the requested mode.
+
+Selection rules:
+- Only `waiting` tickets of the given queue are candidates; other queues and already-called tickets are never selected.
+- Ordering is deterministic: higher `priority` first, then oldest `issued_at`, then lowest `id`.
+- `priority_only` restricts candidates to priority tickets (`priority > 0`); `normal_only` restricts to normal tickets (`priority = 0`, oldest first); `any` uses full ordering plus the fairness rule below.
+- Fairness (`any` only): a normal ticket may not wait behind more than 3 consecutive priority calls. The last 3 tickets called in the queue (most recent first by `called_at`, then by `id`) are inspected; if there are exactly 3, all are priority tickets, and at least one normal ticket is waiting, the call is restricted to normal tickets (the oldest normal is called). Calls made in any mode count toward this history; a normal call resets the streak. If no normal ticket is waiting, priority tickets keep being called.
+- Exactly-once: the queue row is locked, a candidate is picked, then the candidate row is locked and re-checked to still be `waiting`; if it was called concurrently it is skipped and the next candidate is tried.
+- The winner is marked `called` with `called_at = now()` and `called_by_user_id` set, and the updated ticket is returned with those fields already populated. Only `status`, `called_at`, `called_by_user_id` (and `updated_at`) change.
+
+HTTP/Livewire call panels remain future work.
 
